k  like the actors were really interacting  with the dragon  sure it was heavy and bulky but the size  also made it super easy to track and  later  alter with cgi we were able to capture  exactly what he was seeing  and we were going to be able to put that  back on the screen makeup artist and  designer denise kum was responsible for  mulan's incredible matchmaking makeup  but the look was thick  and made facial expressions challenging  each stage was layered with a mix of  pigments  fashion makeup and conventional makeup  and it was all literally painted onto  mulan's face  while mulan cuts her hair in the  animated version designing hair for the  live action version was also  much different and involved applying  tons of hair pieces to leo yaffay's hair  lily james and the live-action  cinderella were in the news a lot over  reports that her waist had been  digitally shrunk in her ball gown but in  reality it was just a very tight and  painful corset  i learned this course it's really hard  to breathe it took 20 minutes to get  lily in  and then out of the dress and corset  which took 20 people to make and  featured 10  000 swarovski crystals and three miles  of hems  princess jasmine has more than 10 outfit  changes during the film  the most painful dress naomi scott had  to wear was this royal pink number  the bodice was tight and restrictive and  it was embellished with heavy gold coins  that the actress had to be careful  not to rattle too much or catch on  anything while moving around  the most challenging costume for emily  blunt to wear as mary poppins was this  dress  while they look like they have ruffles  and fabric details it's all painted on  to blend in with the animation of the  scene  which also affected the way emily had to  wear the costumes  she had to carry them as if they did  have ruffles and voluminous skirts and  make sure her movements didn't make the  dresses fall flat  turning 2d designs into a 3d dress  you won't believe how many of these  actors didn't have any cgi used for  their mcu character  instead they had hours in a makeup chair  which actor had  such intense body makeup and prosthetics  that they literally had to sit in a  sauna so it could melt off  how about the actor who carried an extra  8 pounds of weight on their head alone  cgi magic is impressive but these  extraordinary makeup prosthetic and  costume transformations will blow you  away  when it was time to be in the makeup  chair michael b jordan spent a whole two  and a half hours  every single day having a whopping 90  individual prosthetics glued and sealed  on his body  leaving the actor totally exhausted by  the end of it what's worse is that he  was nowhere near the end of his workday  since he still  actually had to shoot as for the removal  process  well he was stuck in a sauna to help all  the prosthetics actually  sweat off there she is in all her glory  when tom hiddleston put on his loki suit  he was carrying around an extra 30  pounds  add the headpiece an extra 8 pounds  a whopping 40 extra pounds at all times  this large and heavy helmet covers  hiddleston's ears which also limit how  much he was able to actually hear  the suit itself was extremely hot and  sweaty for the actor and with the helmet  well he was facing an overwhelming icky  sweat fest every single day  hiddleston said the whole experience was  uncomfortable and left him feeling  really claustrophobic  where the first piece locks you like  that the second piece zips up and  launches like that and the third piece  is like  the new captain america is here but for  wyatt russell  it's been a long time coming he  auditioned for the role years ago  when he was cast as the new captain he  actually asked if he could wear chris  evans suit  what we see him in here in the falcon in  the winter soldier though is a new  costume made just for him  a hot stiff difficult and painful  costume  it was so bad that an old shoulder  injury of his actually flared up  part of the reason it's so uncomfortable  is because there's supposed to be a  sort of presentational effect have you  ever seen a superhero with bad posture  next time you watch the show remember  that russell is working through  loads of pain every day there's  something that's easier and something  that's harder  she looks good there's no denying that  but at what cost  well tessa thompson knows since she was  the one wearing an almost entirely  plastic outfit  definitely not comfortable or breathable  despite feeling incredibly stiff  hot and always sweating thompson managed  to act her way through it  if that weren't tough enough she also  had her fair share of wire work  discomfort on top of discomfort my  makeup goes on much faster but it's it's  like  glue there actually glue transfers it  then they stick to me  dave bautista spent the end of every  shoot day is drax in asana  not a bad gig right think again he also  had a whopping  5 hours in the makeup chair every single  day getting 18 pieces of prosthetic  attached and makeup done by  5 different makeup artists if that  weren't bad enough  bautista had to stand for the majority  of it with his arms sticking out  how he still had the energy to perform  is a total mystery to us  so how does the sauna fit into all of  this  well when he first had the makeup on  rubbing it off was so tough on his body  that it damaged his skin to the point  that he described it looking like  hamburger meat so the best solution was  to put him in a sauna so the makeup  could just  melt off elizabeth tabiki had a shorter  prep time than many of the other marvel  characters but she still spent a solid  hour and a half with two makeup artists  at work  her prep pretty much involved being  painted and allowing it to dry until she  was ready to get into what was lovingly  called the  aisha taco aka this giant metal gold  dress  while it looks regal and elegant the  costume was made almost  entirely of metal making it super heavy  for 