ven worse is millie  bobby brown's knee injury actually  caused the filming of daker scenes to be  pushed up with barely any notice  the makeup department head amy l  forsythe said i got a call during the  hiatus giving me a heads up about doing  the post sauna scene with billy  on the stairwell getting his wounds  nursed the day after we were to get back  from hiatus  i hadn't even seen a preview for the  sauna fight so i didn't know how he was  getting hurt or where his wounds might  be  i gotta warn you again in your band for  life the duffer brothers were super  adamant about including as many  practical effects as they could in  stranger things which means season one  barely required  any digital visual effects including the  demogorgon  the demogorgon was actually just one big  prosthetic suit that was worn by actor  mark steger  however opting for practical effects  came with some pretty big challenges for  mark  he had to perform some intense stunts in  the suit that he couldn't properly hear  or  see in but he did say that it helped him  remember why he loved film  in the later seasons the duffer brothers  eventually decided to move on to more of  a cgi route  let's just say things got a little too  gooey  it's crazy this is crazy this is crazy  daker loved being able to embrace billy  by adding on his  bad boy characteristics like his tattoo  and scar  however it was at the expense of  spending more time in the makeup chair  after a full day of filming daker would  endure another two hours removing the  prosthetics from his body  including the prosthetics he needed to  cover his facial hair shadow  he wore the prosthetic so much that at  one point he noticed his body hair  wasn't even growing  back anymore every day when you spend  like two hours getting them off  like i remember there was a big cut and  scar right here  you can see i've got no hair on my arm  there because it's just been months and  months of shaving right in that spot  it shouldn't have 